{"duration_api_ms":263693,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"88d1756a-8538-4e67-b745-9c6b4e9e1ce8","total_cost_usd":3.6503639999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":384057,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":28895,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":21971},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":384057,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":28895,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":384057,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":3.6503639999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":21971,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"kind\":\"semantic_stage_assessment_candidate\",\"schemaVersion\":\"5.0.0\",\"criteria\":[{\"criterionRef\":\"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/requirements/source-faithfulness@5\",\"disposition\":\"satisfied\",\"explanation\":\"I compared the 23 statements, 15 candidates and 15 bindings with the supplied 6120-byte source text and the admitted Intent and Product assets. I had no file access, so I did not re-hash anything. I spot-checked the cited quotes against the supplied text and found them exact and unique. I also checked, by length, the byte spans that link candidates to requirement identities. Candidate 01 matches the four spans of 30df46b3. Candidate 02 matches the 50-byte and 49-byte spans of 2e3b657b. Candidate 03 matches the spans of d1008669, and candidate 13 matches the seven spans of deb95e34. Candidate 15's four quotes match the grounded spans of db07c18d (154-174, 180-216, 2867-2942, 5411-5457).\\n\\nThe three defects from the previous falsification are repaired.\\n(1) Candidate 15 restores the typed return-value observation as mandatory, and binding 01 now makes it mandatory rather than conditional. It cites product-pressure:06 and REQ-GLC-WORKSITE-LIFECYCLE-013 accurately: ordered command results plus exactly one typed observation for each declared outcome predicate, inside an ABI-owned F_P turn, with no harness import of the subject module.\\n(2) Candidate 13 restores the source's authority and evidence relations, with direction. The predecessor must exist when the dependent is built, its current digest must be in the dependent's basis, and a predecessor written afterwards to match does not count. The word \\\"prior\\\" in each source instruction grounds this precedence.\\n(3) Statement 20 restates the exact runPath and all eight traversal steps, and it still treats step-to-stage matching as inference.\\n\\nEvery source instruction is represented: the eight file surfaces and the file-less result; the three documents' contents; both verifiers' import, node:test/strict and exact assertion; the plan's command, args, floor, zero-failure match, conditional pass-count ban and assertedReturnValue; the judged fields; the conjunctive acceptance rule; and the TAP-glyph tolerance. I found no invented fact. The whole-file digest matches taskData, and statement 21 discloses that the author did not re-hash. I found no material loss, so statement 22's claim holds. Two minor, non-material imprecisions: statement 16 says the turns \\\"each 'Write only' named files\\\", but the result stage says \\\"Produce no files.\\\"; and statement 14 no longer restates that the subject is distinct from odd_sdlc, though statements 20-21 and candidate 14 still cover this.\",\"sourceQuotes\":[{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"expectedReturnValue: \\\"Hello, world!\\\"\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"assertedReturnValue must be \\\\\\\"Hello, world!\\\\\\\".\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Use the prior conformance_project artifact as the authority.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Use the prior implementation_design artifact as the authority.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Use the prior source artifact summaries as the evidence source.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"prepare_test_execution_surface\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Produce no files.\"}],\"statementRefs\":[\"requirement-statement:01-greeting-return-value\",\"requirement-statement:13-derivation-dependency\",\"requirement-statement:15-declared-outcome-observation\",\"requirement-statement:16-stage-vector-conflict\",\"requirement-statement:20-witness\",\"requirement-statement:21-source-role\",\"requirement-statement:22-revision-reconciliation\"]},{\"criterionRef\":\"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/requirements/modality-and-conflicts@5\",\"disposition\":\"satisfied\",\"explanation\":\"The modality labels are correct. Statements 01-15 are normative, 16-17 conflicting, 18 speculative (depth coverage, neither required nor forbidden) and 19-23 supporting.\\n\\nConflicts are kept without being decided:\\n- The per-turn 'Write only' limits, the 'in this vector' bans, the plan-stage no-execution limit and executeFromPlan: false stay conflicting (statement 16, req-pressure:01).\\n- executeFromPlan's classification as vector mechanism is explicitly labelled an inference (req-pressure:15).\\n- The parityRule stays conflicting and unruled (statement 17, req-pressure:02), and no current evidence is claimed as identical traversal. Its ban on copying odd_sdlc machinery is correctly normative as candidate 14.\\n\\nThe derivation direction moved from an open question to normative. That move is justified: the source says \\\"prior\\\", and the Intent assessor required the dependencies to be kept unless an owner rules otherwise. The remaining sub-question, whether separate sequential activations are needed, stays with the owner.\\n\\nThe source's conditional pass-count ban is now stated conditionally in candidate 10. req-pressure:22 discloses that never pinning a fragment is a permitted conservative choice, not an obligation. 'such as fail 0' stays an example. The direct-return reading is normative with an owner repricing path (req-pressure:07). Whether assertedReturnValue is a separate predicate stays open (req-pressure:06). No acceptor or owner ruling is invented (req-pressure:10). All 17 Product pressures are carried forward with their dispositions.\",\"sourceQuotes\":[{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"reproduce traversal shape as typed GTL vectors consumed by ABG startup\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"do not copy odd_sdlc runtime code, ledgers, phase-flow controller, or local truth surfaces\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"executeFromPlan: false\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"do not pin an exact pass-count fragment when the generated tests add depth coverage\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Write only package.json and src/hello.mjs.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Do not execute the test in this vector.\"}],\"statementRefs\":[\"requirement-statement:10-execution-plan\",\"requirement-statement:13-derivation-dependency\",\"requirement-statement:14-no-copied-predecessor-machinery\",\"requirement-statement:15-declared-outcome-observation\",\"requirement-statement:16-stage-vector-conflict\",\"requirement-statement:17-traversal-parity-conflict\",\"requirement-statement:18-depth-coverage\"]},{\"criterionRef\":\"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/requirements/obligation-conservation@5\",\"disposition\":\"satisfied\",\"explanation\":\"Each of the 15 candidates has exactly one binding to the installed template proof-template://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/behavior@5, with previousVersionRef null. Each binding fills realization, verifier_artifact, verifier_execution and semantic_assessment, repeats the template's required-content line, keeps a non-closing 'Candidate, not ready' rule and lists its unproved scope.\\n\\nThe previous role merge is fixed:\\n- Candidate 11: the run record is the realization, and a separate derivation over it is the verifier_execution.\\n- Candidate 12: the per-suite outcomes are the realization, and an F_D evaluator is the verifier_execution.\\n- Candidate 15: the typed observation is the realization, and a comparison kept apart from the F_P turn is the verifier_execution.\\n\\nThe declared return-value outcome now needs its own typed observation. Passing assertions are explicitly not enough (candidates 01 and 15).\\n\\nOther source obligations are kept:\\n- per-suite attribution\\n- zero failures\\n- the pass floor of at least 2\\n- planSatisfied\\n- the stdout digest\\n- a strict, real-module import, with no stub or copy\\n- document contents\\n- derivation with current digests\\n\\nNo name, count, exit status or declaration closes anything. Gaps are disclosed honestly: the source names no verifier for candidates 02-07, 13 and 14 (req-pressure:18), and a passing run proves nothing about type:module (req-pressure:19).\\n\\nTwo coherence weaknesses remain, both recorded as pressure. Neither drops an obligation. First, bindings 08 and 09 name a design-selected static check as verifier_artifact but give only the planned node --test run as verifier_execution, so the static check has no execution of its own. Second, candidate 15's realization is an observation rather than an authored artifact. The evidence-model question raised in req-pressure:23 applies to it too, but req-pressure:23 covers only 11 and 12.\",\"sourceQuotes\":[{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Accept only if both component and UAT tests passed, planSatisfied is true, and observedTestPassCount is at least the prior test_execution_plan expectedTestPassCount.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Judge the observed executionStatus, planSatisfied flag, observedTestPassCount, and stdout digest against the prior test_execution_plan.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"expectedTestPassCount must be at least 2, matching the admitted component and UAT coverage floor.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Specify both component and UAT validation obligations.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"package.json must be private:true and type:module.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Do not reject solely because node:test uses a different TAP prefix glyph when the F_D pass-count check is satisfied.\"}],\"statementRefs\":[\"requirement-statement:01-greeting-return-value\",\"requirement-statement:02-package-manifest\",\"requirement-statement:08-component-verifier\",\"requirement-statement:09-uat-verifier\",\"requirement-statement:11-observed-execution-result\",\"requirement-statement:12-acceptance-predicate\",\"requirement-statement:13-derivation-dependency\",\"requirement-statement:15-declared-outcome-observation\",\"requirement-statement:19-proof-role-mapping\"]},{\"criterionRef\":\"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/requirements/bounded-claim@5\",\"disposition\":\"satisfied\",\"explanation\":\"The asset claims only requirement candidates and paired binding candidates (statement 23). Every closure rule reads 'Candidate, not ready'. Acceptance stays an owner ruling. The asset claims no release, application closure, continuation or native identity.\\n\\nIt keeps three things apart: construction readiness (req-pressure:24 declines to classify upstream ABI readiness and says any capability that is not ready blocks the dependent edge, with no local compensation); future observed behavior (candidates 11, 12 and 15 describe runs that have not happened); and remaining application obligations (req-pressure:25).\\n\\nThe supplied worksite context is pre-construction, with no revision targets, currentWorksiteDigest null and the observation body omitted. That is consistent with statement 23, which says the supplied context records no subject surface. I could not inventory the worksite independently. Statement 21 honestly says the author used the supplied source without re-hashing it.\",\"sourceQuotes\":[{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Produce no files.\"},{\"memberRef\":\"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4\",\"quote\":\"Judge the observed executionStatus, planSatisfied flag, observedTestPassCount, and stdout digest against the prior test_execution_plan.\"}],\"statementRefs\":[\"requirement-statement:11-observed-execution-result\",\"requirement-statement:12-acceptance-predicate\",\"requirement-statement:21-source-role\",\"requirement-statement:22-revision-reconciliation\",\"requirement-statement:23-stage-claim-boundary\"]}],\"pressure\":[{\"pressureRef\":\"assessment-pressure:01-verifier-artifact-execution-pairing\",\"text\":\"In bindings 08 and 09, the verifier_artifact is a design-selected static check (exact import, node:test and strict import, strict-equality assertion). The only verifier_execution named is the planned node --test run, so nothing executes the static check. Design must add an admitted execution of that check. Otherwise the structural verifier_artifact stays unexercised, and the import and strictness properties rest on semantic assessment alone.\",\"requirementRefs\":[\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/c3c7009cb1e49e23fae21451aa6ad87a43302bf11a516ea6474f53a61dc1dff0\",\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/096d0a714a479913dd0b14ff796f14e94967027f37c7d6d68cf74a65eac382af\"],\"disposition\":\"pending\"},{\"pressureRef\":\"assessment-pressure:02-typed-observation-admission-path\",\"text\":\"Candidate 15's realization is an admitted typed observation, not an authored artifact. req-pressure:23 raises the evidence-model admission question only for candidates 11 and 12, but it applies here too. It is also unassessed whether the installed native-work/observation@5 and command-execution-observation@5 contracts count as the ABI-owned F_P Worker turn that REQ-GLC-WORKSITE-LIFECYCLE-013 requires, one that returns the ordered command results together with exactly one typed helloWorld() observation. If they do not, the dependent edge blocks as an ABI gap.\",\"requirementRefs\":[\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/30df46b3a377bf87e91411f3d718fc8b6264ad38ab14b8e9528db4d8edeaddcf\",\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/47d928d294525d01d84911335c44890240218eddadcd74a77613030f998ce956\"],\"disposition\":\"pending\"},{\"pressureRef\":\"assessment-pressure:03-derivation-implies-sequencing\",\"text\":\"Candidate 13 requires each predecessor's current digest to be in the dependent's admitted construction basis. The declared dependencyRule reads that basis as declared read paths observed before construction. Under that rule, one construction activation that writes both predecessor and dependent may be unable to satisfy candidate 13, which would make sequential activations a consequence rather than an open option. Design must show whether single-activation satisfaction is possible. The owner ruling on per-turn limits (req-pressure:01) stays open.\",\"requirementRefs\":[\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/deb95e344572417adc8634c13e9fb19f007b4da8b838eba744d276ee2f47741c\"],\"disposition\":\"pending\"},{\"pressureRef\":\"assessment-pressure:04-owner-rulings-open\",\"text\":\"These still need an owner ruling, and this assessment grants none:\\n- whether any per-turn write or no-execution limit survives\\n- whether traversal-shape parity is still owed\\n- whether 'artifact summaries' or the artifact bodies form the evidence basis\\n- who the acceptor is\\n- whether the direct-return reading of 'returns exactly' should be repriced\\n- whether assertedReturnValue is a separate declared predicate that needs its own observation\",\"requirementRefs\":[\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/deb95e344572417adc8634c13e9fb19f007b4da8b838eba744d276ee2f47741c\",\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/ec7c71cd55dbe7809d281a122af96a126dbf1342c9506c6afb0b33bd8f87d7be\",\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/6863cc85b10906a717be9be9e25020319457a780da0831e33671d83b992f4ff4\",\"requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/30df46b3a377bf87e91411f3d718fc8b6264ad38ab14b8e9528db4d8edeaddcf\"],\"disposition\":\"conflicting\"},{\"pressureRef\":\"assessment-pressure:05-assessor-verification-limits\",\"text\":\"This assessment rests on the supplied source text, predecessor assets and worksite context. I did not re-hash the source member or predecessor assets, and I did not inventory the worksite. I verified candidate-to-identity span links by length only for candidates 01, 02, 03, 13 and 15. The rest were compared by quote content.\",\"requirementRefs\":[],\"disposition\":\"unassessed\"},{\"pressureRef\":\"assessment-pressure:06-application-obligations-unrealized\",\"text\":\"Every application obligation is still unrealized:\\n- all eight file surfaces, each with its derivation basis\\n- the typed helloWorld() observation\\n- admitted execution of node --test test/component/hello.test.mjs test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs, showing per-suite passes, zero failures, at least 2 passes and plan satisfaction (planSatisfied is not yet defined)\\n- a stdout-match fragment chosen against the real reporter\\n- design-selected checks for candidates 02-07, 13 and 14\\n- independent semantic assessment and the owner acceptance ruling\\n\\nThe readiness of the upstream ABI capabilities has not been classified.\",\"requirementRefs\":[],\"disposition\":\"pending\"}]}","structured_output":{"kind":"semantic_stage_assessment_candidate","schemaVersion":"5.0.0","criteria":[{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/requirements/source-faithfulness@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"I compared the 23 statements, 15 candidates and 15 bindings with the supplied 6120-byte source text and the admitted Intent and Product assets. I had no file access, so I did not re-hash anything. I spot-checked the cited quotes against the supplied text and found them exact and unique. I also checked, by length, the byte spans that link candidates to requirement identities. Candidate 01 matches the four spans of 30df46b3. Candidate 02 matches the 50-byte and 49-byte spans of 2e3b657b. Candidate 03 matches the spans of d1008669, and candidate 13 matches the seven spans of deb95e34. Candidate 15's four quotes match the grounded spans of db07c18d (154-174, 180-216, 2867-2942, 5411-5457).\n\nThe three defects from the previous falsification are repaired.\n(1) Candidate 15 restores the typed return-value observation as mandatory, and binding 01 now makes it mandatory rather than conditional. It cites product-pressure:06 and REQ-GLC-WORKSITE-LIFECYCLE-013 accurately: ordered command results plus exactly one typed observation for each declared outcome predicate, inside an ABI-owned F_P turn, with no harness import of the subject module.\n(2) Candidate 13 restores the source's authority and evidence relations, with direction. The predecessor must exist when the dependent is built, its current digest must be in the dependent's basis, and a predecessor written afterwards to match does not count. The word \"prior\" in each source instruction grounds this precedence.\n(3) Statement 20 restates the exact runPath and all eight traversal steps, and it still treats step-to-stage matching as inference.\n\nEvery source instruction is represented: the eight file surfaces and the file-less result; the three documents' contents; both verifiers' import, node:test/strict and exact assertion; the plan's command, args, floor, zero-failure match, conditional pass-count ban and assertedReturnValue; the judged fields; the conjunctive acceptance rule; and the TAP-glyph tolerance. I found no invented fact. The whole-file digest matches taskData, and statement 21 discloses that the author did not re-hash. I found no material loss, so statement 22's claim holds. Two minor, non-material imprecisions: statement 16 says the turns \"each 'Write only' named files\", but the result stage says \"Produce no files.\"; and statement 14 no longer restates that the subject is distinct from odd_sdlc, though statements 20-21 and candidate 14 still cover this.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"expectedReturnValue: \"Hello, world!\""},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"assertedReturnValue must be \\\"Hello, world!\\\"."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Use the prior conformance_project artifact as the authority."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Use the prior implementation_design artifact as the authority."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Use the prior source artifact summaries as the evidence source."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"prepare_test_execution_surface"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Produce no files."}],"statementRefs":["requirement-statement:01-greeting-return-value","requirement-statement:13-derivation-dependency","requirement-statement:15-declared-outcome-observation","requirement-statement:16-stage-vector-conflict","requirement-statement:20-witness","requirement-statement:21-source-role","requirement-statement:22-revision-reconciliation"]},{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/requirements/modality-and-conflicts@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"The modality labels are correct. Statements 01-15 are normative, 16-17 conflicting, 18 speculative (depth coverage, neither required nor forbidden) and 19-23 supporting.\n\nConflicts are kept without being decided:\n- The per-turn 'Write only' limits, the 'in this vector' bans, the plan-stage no-execution limit and executeFromPlan: false stay conflicting (statement 16, req-pressure:01).\n- executeFromPlan's classification as vector mechanism is explicitly labelled an inference (req-pressure:15).\n- The parityRule stays conflicting and unruled (statement 17, req-pressure:02), and no current evidence is claimed as identical traversal. Its ban on copying odd_sdlc machinery is correctly normative as candidate 14.\n\nThe derivation direction moved from an open question to normative. That move is justified: the source says \"prior\", and the Intent assessor required the dependencies to be kept unless an owner rules otherwise. The remaining sub-question, whether separate sequential activations are needed, stays with the owner.\n\nThe source's conditional pass-count ban is now stated conditionally in candidate 10. req-pressure:22 discloses that never pinning a fragment is a permitted conservative choice, not an obligation. 'such as fail 0' stays an example. The direct-return reading is normative with an owner repricing path (req-pressure:07). Whether assertedReturnValue is a separate predicate stays open (req-pressure:06). No acceptor or owner ruling is invented (req-pressure:10). All 17 Product pressures are carried forward with their dispositions.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"reproduce traversal shape as typed GTL vectors consumed by ABG startup"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"do not copy odd_sdlc runtime code, ledgers, phase-flow controller, or local truth surfaces"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"executeFromPlan: false"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"do not pin an exact pass-count fragment when the generated tests add depth coverage"},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Write only package.json and src/hello.mjs."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Do not execute the test in this vector."}],"statementRefs":["requirement-statement:10-execution-plan","requirement-statement:13-derivation-dependency","requirement-statement:14-no-copied-predecessor-machinery","requirement-statement:15-declared-outcome-observation","requirement-statement:16-stage-vector-conflict","requirement-statement:17-traversal-parity-conflict","requirement-statement:18-depth-coverage"]},{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/requirements/obligation-conservation@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"Each of the 15 candidates has exactly one binding to the installed template proof-template://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/behavior@5, with previousVersionRef null. Each binding fills realization, verifier_artifact, verifier_execution and semantic_assessment, repeats the template's required-content line, keeps a non-closing 'Candidate, not ready' rule and lists its unproved scope.\n\nThe previous role merge is fixed:\n- Candidate 11: the run record is the realization, and a separate derivation over it is the verifier_execution.\n- Candidate 12: the per-suite outcomes are the realization, and an F_D evaluator is the verifier_execution.\n- Candidate 15: the typed observation is the realization, and a comparison kept apart from the F_P turn is the verifier_execution.\n\nThe declared return-value outcome now needs its own typed observation. Passing assertions are explicitly not enough (candidates 01 and 15).\n\nOther source obligations are kept:\n- per-suite attribution\n- zero failures\n- the pass floor of at least 2\n- planSatisfied\n- the stdout digest\n- a strict, real-module import, with no stub or copy\n- document contents\n- derivation with current digests\n\nNo name, count, exit status or declaration closes anything. Gaps are disclosed honestly: the source names no verifier for candidates 02-07, 13 and 14 (req-pressure:18), and a passing run proves nothing about type:module (req-pressure:19).\n\nTwo coherence weaknesses remain, both recorded as pressure. Neither drops an obligation. First, bindings 08 and 09 name a design-selected static check as verifier_artifact but give only the planned node --test run as verifier_execution, so the static check has no execution of its own. Second, candidate 15's realization is an observation rather than an authored artifact. The evidence-model question raised in req-pressure:23 applies to it too, but req-pressure:23 covers only 11 and 12.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Accept only if both component and UAT tests passed, planSatisfied is true, and observedTestPassCount is at least the prior test_execution_plan expectedTestPassCount."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Judge the observed executionStatus, planSatisfied flag, observedTestPassCount, and stdout digest against the prior test_execution_plan."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"expectedTestPassCount must be at least 2, matching the admitted component and UAT coverage floor."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Specify both component and UAT validation obligations."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"package.json must be private:true and type:module."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Do not reject solely because node:test uses a different TAP prefix glyph when the F_D pass-count check is satisfied."}],"statementRefs":["requirement-statement:01-greeting-return-value","requirement-statement:02-package-manifest","requirement-statement:08-component-verifier","requirement-statement:09-uat-verifier","requirement-statement:11-observed-execution-result","requirement-statement:12-acceptance-predicate","requirement-statement:13-derivation-dependency","requirement-statement:15-declared-outcome-observation","requirement-statement:19-proof-role-mapping"]},{"criterionRef":"criterion://odd-glc/generic-lifecycle/requirements/bounded-claim@5","disposition":"satisfied","explanation":"The asset claims only requirement candidates and paired binding candidates (statement 23). Every closure rule reads 'Candidate, not ready'. Acceptance stays an owner ruling. The asset claims no release, application closure, continuation or native identity.\n\nIt keeps three things apart: construction readiness (req-pressure:24 declines to classify upstream ABI readiness and says any capability that is not ready blocks the dependent edge, with no local compensation); future observed behavior (candidates 11, 12 and 15 describe runs that have not happened); and remaining application obligations (req-pressure:25).\n\nThe supplied worksite context is pre-construction, with no revision targets, currentWorksiteDigest null and the observation body omitted. That is consistent with statement 23, which says the supplied context records no subject surface. I could not inventory the worksite independently. Statement 21 honestly says the author used the supplied source without re-hashing it.","sourceQuotes":[{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Produce no files."},{"memberRef":"urn:sha256:c799b9e43d660f3abc3adf0da32baab17a771f1efe20843c4688162b9e62ced4","quote":"Judge the observed executionStatus, planSatisfied flag, observedTestPassCount, and stdout digest against the prior test_execution_plan."}],"statementRefs":["requirement-statement:11-observed-execution-result","requirement-statement:12-acceptance-predicate","requirement-statement:21-source-role","requirement-statement:22-revision-reconciliation","requirement-statement:23-stage-claim-boundary"]}],"pressure":[{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:01-verifier-artifact-execution-pairing","text":"In bindings 08 and 09, the verifier_artifact is a design-selected static check (exact import, node:test and strict import, strict-equality assertion). The only verifier_execution named is the planned node --test run, so nothing executes the static check. Design must add an admitted execution of that check. Otherwise the structural verifier_artifact stays unexercised, and the import and strictness properties rest on semantic assessment alone.","requirementRefs":["requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/c3c7009cb1e49e23fae21451aa6ad87a43302bf11a516ea6474f53a61dc1dff0","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/096d0a714a479913dd0b14ff796f14e94967027f37c7d6d68cf74a65eac382af"],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:02-typed-observation-admission-path","text":"Candidate 15's realization is an admitted typed observation, not an authored artifact. req-pressure:23 raises the evidence-model admission question only for candidates 11 and 12, but it applies here too. It is also unassessed whether the installed native-work/observation@5 and command-execution-observation@5 contracts count as the ABI-owned F_P Worker turn that REQ-GLC-WORKSITE-LIFECYCLE-013 requires, one that returns the ordered command results together with exactly one typed helloWorld() observation. If they do not, the dependent edge blocks as an ABI gap.","requirementRefs":["requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/30df46b3a377bf87e91411f3d718fc8b6264ad38ab14b8e9528db4d8edeaddcf","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/47d928d294525d01d84911335c44890240218eddadcd74a77613030f998ce956"],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:03-derivation-implies-sequencing","text":"Candidate 13 requires each predecessor's current digest to be in the dependent's admitted construction basis. The declared dependencyRule reads that basis as declared read paths observed before construction. Under that rule, one construction activation that writes both predecessor and dependent may be unable to satisfy candidate 13, which would make sequential activations a consequence rather than an open option. Design must show whether single-activation satisfaction is possible. The owner ruling on per-turn limits (req-pressure:01) stays open.","requirementRefs":["requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/deb95e344572417adc8634c13e9fb19f007b4da8b838eba744d276ee2f47741c"],"disposition":"pending"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:04-owner-rulings-open","text":"These still need an owner ruling, and this assessment grants none:\n- whether any per-turn write or no-execution limit survives\n- whether traversal-shape parity is still owed\n- whether 'artifact summaries' or the artifact bodies form the evidence basis\n- who the acceptor is\n- whether the direct-return reading of 'returns exactly' should be repriced\n- whether assertedReturnValue is a separate declared predicate that needs its own observation","requirementRefs":["requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/deb95e344572417adc8634c13e9fb19f007b4da8b838eba744d276ee2f47741c","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/ec7c71cd55dbe7809d281a122af96a126dbf1342c9506c6afb0b33bd8f87d7be","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/6863cc85b10906a717be9be9e25020319457a780da0831e33671d83b992f4ff4","requirement://abiogenesis/semantic-job/30df46b3a377bf87e91411f3d718fc8b6264ad38ab14b8e9528db4d8edeaddcf"],"disposition":"conflicting"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:05-assessor-verification-limits","text":"This assessment rests on the supplied source text, predecessor assets and worksite context. I did not re-hash the source member or predecessor assets, and I did not inventory the worksite. I verified candidate-to-identity span links by length only for candidates 01, 02, 03, 13 and 15. The rest were compared by quote content.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"unassessed"},{"pressureRef":"assessment-pressure:06-application-obligations-unrealized","text":"Every application obligation is still unrealized:\n- all eight file surfaces, each with its derivation basis\n- the typed helloWorld() observation\n- admitted execution of node --test test/component/hello.test.mjs test/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs, showing per-suite passes, zero failures, at least 2 passes and plan satisfaction (planSatisfied is not yet defined)\n- a stdout-match fragment chosen against the real reporter\n- design-selected checks for candidates 02-07, 13 and 14\n- independent semantic assessment and the owner acceptance ruling\n\nThe readiness of the upstream ABI capabilities has not been classified.","requirementRefs":[],"disposition":"pending"}]},"ttft_ms":210822,"type":"result","duration_ms":271981,"uuid":"ec8115bc-9f45-444c-bf5f-2f721e651b41","ttft_stream_ms":13327,"time_to_request_ms":8286,"first_content_frame_ms":13328,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
